    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n107351" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπερβολ-ικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>hyperbolical, extravagant,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				18.46.13
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑ. σχήματα</span>
			<i>exaggerated</i> attitudes, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				18(2).57
			</span></i>: fem. as Subst., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μηδεμίαν
				ὑπερβολικὴν ποιουμένοις</span> committing no
				<i>extravagance,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Milet.
				7.69
			</span></i> (Didyma, <span class="entity">ii B. C.</span>). Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς, ὑ. ἀποφαίνεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					2.62.9
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Mus.</u>
				p.72
			</span></i> K., <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				17(2).209
			</span></i>, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ώτερον εἰπεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					7.11.8
				</span></i>
			.</div>
